Schema:
Entity-relationship Diagram
Entities {User, Loan_Request, Active_Loan, Matched_Request Dispute, Activity_Log, Transaction}


Relationships (with Cardinalities)
1.	User(client) (1) approved (0..1) User(Admin)
2.	User(client) (1) submits (0..*) Loan_Request
3.	User(Admin) (1) Approves (0..*) Loan_Request
4.	User(Investor)(0..*) matches (0..*) Loan_Request
5.	User(Client, Investor)(1) raises (0..*)Dispute
6.	User(1) makes (0..*) transaction
7.	User(1)generates (1..*)Activity_log  
8.	User(1) related (1..*) Matched_Request 

9.	Loan_Request(1) relates (0..*) matched_request
o	Loan request can be matched zero or more times
10.	Loan_Request(1) becomes (1) Active_Loan

11.	Active_Loan(1) related (1..*)matched_Request
12.	Active_Loan(1) relates (1)Dispute
13.	Active_Loan(1) relates (0..*)Transaction

Entity-Relationship Diagram

Entities (with key attributes)
1. User
•	user_id (PK)
•	email
•	password_hash
•	full_name
•	phone_number
•	address
•	credit_score
•	role (User, Admin, SuperAdmin)
•	permissions(can_borrow,can_invest)
•	account_status (pending, Active, Suspended)
•	registration_date
•	approved_by (FK to Admin who approved)
2. Loan_Request
•	request_id (PK)
•	borrower_id (FK to User)
•	requested_amount
•	description
•	term_months
•	interest_rate
•	amount_Funded
•	state(pending_approval, approved, rejected)
•	status (not_Funded, partialy_funded, fully_funded, disbursed, expired)
•	request_date
•	dead_line
•	approval_id (FK to Admin who approved/rejected)


3. Matched¬_Request
•	match_id (PK)
•	request_id (FK to Loan_Request)
•	investor_id(FK to User)
•	invested_amount
•	match_date
4. Active_Loan////////////
•	active_loan_id (PK)
•	loan_request_id (FK to Loan_Request)
•	lender_id (FK to User)
•	borrower_id (FK to User)
•	principal_remaining
•	next_payment_due_date
•	start_date
•	status (Active, Completed, Defaulted)
5. Transaction
•	transaction_id (PK)
•	user_id (FK to User)
•	active_loan_id (FK)
•	amount
•	type (Loan Payment, Disbursement, Investment_Deposit)
•	payment_method
•	status (Pending, Completed, Failed)
•	transaction_date
6. Dispute
•	dispute_id (PK)
•	raised_by (FK to User)
•	active_loan_id (FK)
•	reason
•	description
•	status (Open, Under Review, Resolved, Closed)
•	resolution_notes
•	created_date
•	resolved_by (FK to Admin)
7. Activity_Log
•	log_id (PK)
•	user_id (FK to User)
•	action
•	ip_address
•	timestamp
•	details (JSON or Text)

